## T-406 — PROJ_RIVE-GO_CODE_V1_COMPLETE
Date: 2026-05-10

### Draw Order Rules API

Implemented Draw Order Rules (DrawTarget typeKey=48, DrawRules typeKey=49) in the
goriv builder. Shapes can now declare explicit draw-order constraints independent
of their declaration order in the children list.

### Files changed
- `rive/builder/drawrule.go` — new: PlacementAbove/Below constants, drawRuleConfig struct
- `rive/builder/shape.go` — added drawRules field, DrawAbove/DrawBelow methods, emitDrawRules()
- `rive/builder/builder.go` — post-pass in emit() to call emitDrawRules after all shapes
- `rive/builder/props.go` — added PropDrawableId=119, PropPlacementValue=120, PropDrawTargetId=121
- `rive/builder/drawrule_test.go` — 5 new tests (above/below/multi/round-trip/no-rules)
- `rive/fromjson/fromjson.go` — Child.DrawRules []DrawRuleDef, applied in buildScene post-pass
- `docs/preview/fromjson/draw_order_demo.json` — demo scene
- `docs/preview/fromjson_draw_order.riv` — compiled (299 bytes)
- `docs/preview/index.html` — preview card added, count updated to seven
- `cmd/rivtool/main.go` — DrawTarget/DrawRules added to typeKeyName map

### Design notes
- Draw rules use a deferred post-pass (after all shapes) so all shapeIdx values are set
- DrawTarget.ParentId=0 → artboard root sibling (suppressed by Component.Properties)
- DrawRules.ParentId = source.shapeIdx (child of source shape)
- Fluent API: shape.DrawAbove(target).DrawBelow(other) (chainable)
- fromjson: draw_rules array on child, applied after nameMap is fully populated

### All tests pass

