## T-407 — PROJ_RIVE-GO_CODE_V2_COMPLETE
Date: 2026-05-10

### Animated Draw Order (Hold Keyframes on DrawRules)

Implemented animated draw order: hold keyframes that switch DrawRules.drawTargetId
(key=121) at specific animation frames, using KeyFrameId (typeKey=50).

### Files changed
- `rive/builder/anim.go` — drawOrderKF struct, drawOrderKFs field on AnimationBuilder,
  KeyframeDrawOrder() method, animated draw order pre-pass in emit() (DrawTarget+DrawRules
  objects emitted before LinearAnimation so indices are known), draw order keyframe
  emission section at end of emit()
- `rive/builder/draworder_anim_test.go` — 5 new tests
- `rive/fromjson/fromjson.go` — DrawOrderTrackDef + DrawOrderKFDef types added to
  AnimationDef; parse and apply in buildScene after regular tracks
- `docs/preview/fromjson/draw_order_anim_demo.json` — ball passes through panel
- `docs/preview/fromjson_draw_order_anim.riv` — compiled (254 bytes)
- `docs/preview/index.html` — preview card added, count updated to eight
- `cmd/rivtool/main.go` — KeyFrameId (typeKey=50) named in inspector

### Design notes
- DrawTarget+DrawRules for animated rules emitted BEFORE LinearAnimation in emit()
  so artboard-relative indices are stable when emitting KeyFrameId values
- KeyFrameId.Value = DrawTarget artboard-relative index, or ^uint64(0) for "no rule"
- InterpolationType=0 (hold) is the implicit default (suppressed from binary)
- Multiple (target, placement) pairs per source shape each get their own DrawTarget
- Static draw rules (from T-406) and animated draw rules coexist on the same shape

### All tests pass (10 packages)

